cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "Cite this repository for the pipeline and notes. Cite the papers below for the methods."
title: "Fragment-based sample-based quantum diagonalization on ammonia (6-31G)"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-09
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Reddy
    given-names: Santhosh
abstract: "A tutorial that compares exact FCI, whole-molecule SQD and fragment SQD on NH3 in 6-31G, tests the circuit against free classical baselines at matched subspace size, adds one gateway run and three IBM hardware jobs, and ends with a water-dimer study whose pre-registered target was not met. Includes negative results."
keywords: [ammonia, water dimer, fragmentation, embedding, SQD, FCI, Qiskit, IBM Quantum]
references:
  - type: article
    title: "Demonstration of Parallel Multi-QPU Execution for Fragment-Based Quantum Chemistry Using On-Premises Hardware"
    authors:
      - family-names: Herrmann
        given-names: Nils
    notes: "arXiv:2610.07702 (first author listed; see the paper for the full list)"
  - type: article
    title: "Quantum Computations on Fusion Blanket Molten Salts"
    authors:
      - family-names: Das
        given-names: Susanta
    notes: "arXiv:2606.30402 (first author listed; see the paper for the full list)"
